 "diagnosis": {
  "firstRound": "evidence raw/ preserved untouched: five SSH-driven cases ERROR with SOPS_TRANSPORT_ERROR (stage RESTRICTED_SSH_RUNNER, scannerStarted=false); data-drift COMPLETED/FAIL; disabled cases normal; cross-project rejections normal; Loki FAILED/NOT_VERIFIED for the two ERROR runs.",
  "rootCause": "devops auth log shows the five failed sessions each lasted ~20.3s - exactly the entry run_tool default timeout (20s). A subprocess inside the entry (the sops --version online update check, run in a stripped environment without proxy) stalled past 20s; subprocess.TimeoutExpired was not caught by the entry (only RuntimeError was), so the entry died with a traceback and no JSON packet, which the runner correctly mapped to SOPS_TRANSPORT_ERROR. The one success (data-drift, 16.6s) finished the same check just under the timeout. The entry, user, authorized_keys forced command and pinned tool hashes were all already in place and correct.",
  "fixes": [
   "entry.py: sops --version probe now uses timeout=6 and falls back to the pinned sha256 (verified separately at entry start) on any probe failure.",
   "entry.py: top-level subprocess.TimeoutExpired now returns a JSON {error: EXECUTION_TIMEOUT, stages} packet instead of a traceback.",
   "entry.py: tampered-ciphertext now flips one base64 character inside the encrypted payload (JSON structure, sops metadata and MAC field intact) instead of a whole-file midpoint byte flip, which had randomly corrupted the JSON structure depending on the random ciphertext (rerun attempt 1: RUNNER_REPORT_ERROR)."
  ]
 },
